Marcus / David,

Routine preventive maintenance was completed on the Deckel Maho CNC vertical machining center spindle unit this morning.

Service Notes:
1. Spindle ceramic hybrid ball bearings inspected: no cage damage or spalling observed.
2. Klüber high-speed spindle grease replenished (6.5 ml per bearing pocket).
3. Motor current draw test at 1600 rpm no-load speed stabilized at 1.85 A (well below the 3.5 A safety trip limit).
4. Thermal sensor at front spindle bearing stabilized at 32.4°C after 30-minute test run.

The machine spindle is certified ready for continuous Latin Square experimental runs across conditions 1 through 25.

